        <body>
            <div xml:id="d43">

                <pb facs="0154" n="58" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg58"/>

                <head>No. 41.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Jones
                        to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-03-22"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 22, 1874</date>.
                        (Received April 7.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 231.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith the
                    report of the commission charged with the examination of the question of
                    extradition, as published in the Moniteur of this date.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. JONES.</signed></closer>




